**Skip the host check for URLs that have no network host.**

For `fetch('data:text/plain,hi')`, `new URL(...).hostname` is an empty string. `local('')` returns false, so `check('')` throws `TEST_EGRESS_BLOCKED`. A `blob:` URL has the same problem. These schemes make no network request, so the guard rejects safe calls and the error message names an empty host. Check the protocol before the host. Only `http:`, `https:`, `ws:` and `wss:` URLs need the host check. Redirect handling is not affected, because the socket-layer patch still covers it.





<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
     const url = new URL(typeof input === 'string' || input instanceof URL ? input : input.url);
-    check(url.hostname);
+    if (!['data:', 'blob:'].includes(url.protocol)) check(url.hostname);
```
</details>
